---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../config/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About End of Day | WARDOGS Community"
  description="End of Day (EOD) is a WARDOGS community founded in 2026 around teamwork, good fights, active administration, and a laid-back community."
>
  <header class="topbar shell">
    <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="End of Day home">
      <span class="brand-logo-frame" aria-hidden="true">
        <img src="/images/end-of-day-logo.png" alt="" />
      </span>
      <span class="brand-copy">
        <strong>END OF DAY</strong>
        <small>EOD • WARDOGS COMMUNITY</small>
      </span>
    </a>

    <nav class="desktop-nav" aria-label="Page navigation">
      <a href="/wardogs-community">COMMUNITY</a>
      <a href="/server">SERVER</a>
      <a href="/about">ABOUT</a>
      <a href="/rules">RULES</a>
      <a class="nav-button" href="/discord">DISCORD</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main class="subpage shell">
    <section class="subpage-heading">
      <p class="section-index">EOD / ABOUT</p>
      <h1>END<br /><em>OF DAY.</em></h1>
      <p>
        End of Day is a WARDOGS community founded in 2026. We're building a
        home server around a simple idea: play hard, work together, and don't
        make the game miserable for everybody else.
        <a class="inline-link" href="/wardogs-community">Read the full EOD community pitch.</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-manifesto">
      <div>
        <p class="section-index">WHY EOD</p>
        <h2>A SERVER SHOULD<br />FEEL LIKE A PLACE.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Anonymous matchmaking is fine, but the best multiplayer servers become
        communities. You recognize the pilot who always gets you there. You know
        which squad is dangerous. Rivalries develop. People teach new players.
        You log in because you know who's going to be there.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-values">
      <article>
        <span>01</span>
        <strong>TEAMWORK WITHOUT BUREAUCRACY</strong>
        <p>Coordinate and help the team. No fake chain of command required.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>02</span>
        <strong>COMPETITIVE WITHOUT BEING MISERABLE</strong>
        <p>We want good fights and players who care about winning without turning every loss into drama.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>03</span>
        <strong>COMMUNITY BEFORE NUMBERS</strong>
        <p>A hundred anonymous members matter less than a smaller group that actually plays together.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>04</span>
        <strong>ACTIVE ADMINISTRATION</strong>
        <p>If we're going to run a server, we're going to take care of it.</p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <div class="subpage-cta">
      <div>
        <small>EST. 2026</small>
        <p>Get in before everybody knows the name.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="button button-accent" href={site.discordUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        JOIN END OF DAY
      </a>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
